From 4708689fb80a87fef3e01bb7bc9c9b3986ed5352 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:32:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] tests/color: Add a test hook at asynchronous color
 callback boundaries

The shutdown ordering fixed by the previous commit depends on exactly
when an asynchronous result is delivered relative to disposal, which a
test cannot control through the normal main loop.

Add an optional hook, compiled only into builds with tests
(HAVE_COLOR_LIFECYCLE_TESTS), at the start of the asynchronous
callbacks of the color manager, device, profile and store. When a test
installs it, it can park a delivery before the callback takes ownership
of anything, and replay the same callback later, after tearing down the
objects involved. Without a hook installed the callbacks run as before.
The hook and its setter are exported for tests only.

Link: TBD-MR
